@startuml
title Level loading R1 — experimento local, no ratificado
hide empty members
package ar.edu.uade.sokoban.level {
  class Position <<record>> {
    -row : int
    -column : int
    +row() : int
    +column() : int
  }
  enum Terrain {
    WALL
    FLOOR
    GOAL
  }
  enum Occupant {
    EMPTY
    PLAYER
    BOX
  }
  class Cell <<record>> {
    -terrain : Terrain
    -occupant : Occupant
    +terrain() : Terrain
    +occupant() : Occupant
  }
  class Board <<record>> {
    {static} +MAX_DIMENSION : int = 100
    -rows : List<List<Cell>>
    +rows() : List<List<Cell>>
    +width() : int
    +height() : int
    +cellAt(position : Position) : Cell
    +playerPosition() : Position
    +boxCount() : long
    +goalCount() : long
  }
  class Level <<record>> {
    -board : Board
    +board() : Board
  }
  class LevelBuilder <<internal>> {
    -rows : List<List<Cell>>
    -published : boolean
    ~addRow(row : List<Cell>) : void
    ~build() : Level
  }
  class LevelParser {
    +parse(text : String) : Level
  }
  class LevelLoader {
    {static} +MAX_FILE_BYTES : int = 65536
    -parser : LevelParser
    +LevelLoader(parser : LevelParser)
    +load(path : Path) : Level
  }
  class LevelFormatException
}
class "IllegalArgumentException (JDK)" as IllegalArgumentException
IllegalArgumentException <|-- LevelFormatException
LevelLoader --> LevelParser
LevelParser ..> LevelBuilder : per load
LevelParser ..> Cell : decodes
LevelBuilder ..> Level : assembles
LevelBuilder ..> Board : validates on construction
Level --> "1" Board : immutable value
Board --> "1..*" Cell : immutable rows
Cell --> Terrain
Cell --> Occupant
Board ..> Position
LevelParser ..> LevelFormatException
LevelBuilder ..> LevelFormatException
LevelLoader ..> LevelFormatException
Board ..> LevelFormatException
note bottom of LevelBuilder
Concrete/internal; no Builder interface or alternate builders.
D-011 remains PREFERRED. Direct construction stays an alternative.
end note
note bottom of Level
Immutable initial product only; no gameplay or Swing.
OQ-08 / OQ-11 remain OPEN. Separate from integral candidate v0.5.
Record constructors validate values; accessors expose immutable data.
Associations do not require exclusive identity ownership.
end note
note bottom of LevelParser
Early dimensions/rectangularity checks bound assembly work.
Board keeps the same final invariants for direct construction.
end note
@enduml
